      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-63528",
      ":question/problem": "A fisherman's boat is $2km$ deep into the sea. An observer on the shores uses the number $-2km$ to describe the location of the fisherman's boat in the sea.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. In this context, $0$ represents the distance of the observer to the shoreline\n2. The absolute value of the location of the fisherman's boat gives the overall distance between the boat and the observer\n3. If a second fisherman's boat is at $-3km$ then he is further from the shore than the first one."
