      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-93571",
      ":question/problem": "A soil scientist located two types of soil, soil $A$ and soil $B$, beneath the ground.\n\nSoil $A$ is located $10m$ below ground level. He records the location of soil $A$ as $-10m$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. In this context, $0m$ represents the location of ground level.\n2. The absolute value of the location of soil $A$ gives the depth of this soil from ground level.\n3. If soil $B$ has a location of $-50m$ and is directly below soil $A$, then soil $A$ is $40m$ above soil $B$."
    }
